                <pb facs="0917" n="827" xml:id="pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3831/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Belden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-05T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5,
                                1920—noon.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 6—1:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>25. Department’s number 32, March 29, noon. Decree has not been issued. The
                    President has instructed Haitian Chargé d’Affaires at Washington to confer with
                    Financial Adviser relative thereto.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Belden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
